        "A **magnetic signature** is the combination of magnetic parameters characteristic of a location. Lohmann and colleagues reproduced three fields from the North Atlantic route, each built from inclination and intensity values that occur together in widely separated oceanic regions. The three fields differed in how inclination and intensity combined. Each signature is a regional magnetic fingerprint of one place.",
        "In the northern Florida field, tethered hatchlings oriented east-southeast. In the northeastern gyre field they swam roughly south, and in the southern gyre field they swam west-northwest. The apparatus recorded heading while the animals stayed in one laboratory arena, so each heading was measured in the same setting. Heading was recorded continuously in each field.",
