        "One interpretation is an inherited large-scale map. A simpler alternative is a set of field-triggered instructions, such as swim south under one signature and west-northwest under another. Both accounts predict the local heading changes, but the map account is the one that requires a general representation of geographical position. The distinction matters for how navigation is organized.",
