        "The tested interval covers months in captivity, far shorter than the years between a hatchling's departure and an adult turtle's return to a nesting region. The retention result sets a measured duration of memory under captive conditions. It reflects a memory that stayed available for months without any reinforcement in between. Captivity was the only setting tested.",
